WEBVTT

00:17.023 --> 00:19.735
- [music playing distantly]
- [people chattering]

00:21.278 --> 00:23.447
[exclaims excitedly]

00:23.530 --> 00:25.532
[young Toshiro gasps]
I know what I wanna do.

00:26.158 --> 00:27.993
I'm gonna be a musician!

00:28.910 --> 00:31.621
Huh? That's so stupid.

00:31.705 --> 00:33.123
[laughs]

00:33.999 --> 00:35.625
[young Toshiro vocalizing]

00:42.632 --> 00:44.509
You can't be serious. That won't happen.

00:44.593 --> 00:46.470
Yeah, I will! Just wait and see!

00:46.553 --> 00:48.346
I'll have to get a part-time job
in middle school,

00:48.430 --> 00:50.891
buy a guitar, and then write 100 songs
by high school.

00:50.974 --> 00:52.267
That's so stupid.

00:52.350 --> 00:54.186
It wasn't even a nice guitar.

00:54.269 --> 00:56.271
How much do you think it costs anyway?

00:57.272 --> 00:58.940
[imitates guitar strumming, laughs]

00:59.024 --> 01:00.776
Next up is the best band in the world!

01:00.859 --> 01:05.614
We've got Toshiro Kamiya on vocals
and Yomiko Horai on bass!

01:05.697 --> 01:07.157
[young Yomiko] Yeah, not happening.

01:08.200 --> 01:10.368
- [loud clanging]
- [young Toshiro vocalizing]

01:10.452 --> 01:11.870
[young Toshiro chuckles]

01:12.412 --> 01:13.580
Definitely not.

01:13.663 --> 01:15.540
[Toshiro scatting]

01:17.292 --> 01:18.418
[laughing]

01:18.919 --> 01:20.420
[imitates guitar lead]

01:23.173 --> 01:24.257
I'm hungry.

01:24.341 --> 01:26.885
I wonder what my mom's making
for dinner tonight.

01:28.553 --> 01:30.013
[young Yomiko sobbing]

01:30.096 --> 01:31.598
What's wrong, Yomiko?

01:31.681 --> 01:33.767
[young Yomiko sniffling]

01:36.353 --> 01:38.355
Found out that I'm switching schools.

01:39.064 --> 01:40.315
[young Toshiro] <i>Yomiko?</i>

01:40.857 --> 01:44.277
[Yomiko] <i>A hundred years have passed since</i>
<i>thick clouds blocked out the sunlight.</i>

01:44.361 --> 01:47.489
<i>Winter and night persist,</i>
<i>so most plants have withered away.</i>

01:47.572 --> 01:48.573
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

01:48.657 --> 01:49.825
<i>In order to survive in this world,</i>

01:49.908 --> 01:51.868
<i>humanity developed</i>
<i>a revolutionary technology</i>

01:51.952 --> 01:53.829
<i>known as Transfloration.</i>

01:53.912 --> 01:56.289
<i>By implanting a Seed</i>
<i>into someone nearing death,</i>

01:56.373 --> 01:58.959
<i>a plant can grow</i>
<i>by feeding on the host's body.</i>

01:59.042 --> 02:00.460
<i>Over the course of roughly two years…</i>

02:00.544 --> 02:01.419
BECOMING A SPIRIFLOR

02:01.503 --> 02:03.672
<i>…those who undergo Transfloration</i>
<i>gradually transform</i>

02:03.755 --> 02:05.924
<i>into trees, flowers, and other plants</i>

02:06.007 --> 02:07.551
<i>which are all called Spiriflora.</i>

02:07.634 --> 02:09.511
<i>Requiring a small amount of light,</i>

02:09.594 --> 02:11.596
<i>Spiriflora produce</i>
<i>large amounts of oxygen,</i>

02:11.680 --> 02:12.722
<i>helping us survive.</i>

02:12.806 --> 02:14.141
[nurse] Yomiko, do you need the forceps?

02:14.224 --> 02:15.308
[Yomiko] No, thanks. I'm good.

02:16.226 --> 02:18.228
All right, we're done. I'm gonna go.
Can you stitch them up?

02:22.774 --> 02:24.693
I feel like we just killed someone.

02:24.776 --> 02:27.362
What do you mean?
We just extended their life.

02:27.445 --> 02:28.613
They were terminally ill.

02:28.697 --> 02:30.448
They would have died in a month
as a human.

02:30.532 --> 02:33.326
[doctor] Are they really living
if they're turning into a plant?

02:33.410 --> 02:35.078
I couldn't care less about that.

02:35.162 --> 02:37.873
It's up to the person whether they want
to undergo the procedure or not.

02:37.956 --> 02:38.790
TRANSFLORATION SUBSIDY

02:38.874 --> 02:41.168
And with the 10 million they get
from the Transfloration Subsidy,

02:41.251 --> 02:43.378
they can live comfortably
during their last two years.

02:47.090 --> 02:49.593
[water droplet plopping]

02:54.723 --> 02:56.099
[rhythmic metal tapping]

02:56.182 --> 02:57.309
[munching]

03:00.312 --> 03:01.646
[tapping continues]

03:03.523 --> 03:04.691
That's how it must be.

03:04.774 --> 03:06.943
I know it is. I know everything.

03:07.027 --> 03:08.737
No one else knows. Only me.

03:08.820 --> 03:10.238
I'm the only one who can tell.

03:10.322 --> 03:12.908
- [sighs in exasperation]
- I won't lose to them. They can't beat me.

03:12.991 --> 03:15.035
I'll never lose. Never, never,
never, never, never, never.

03:15.118 --> 03:15.952
ORAL MEDICATION

03:16.036 --> 03:18.204
- [Toshiro] We ran out yesterday.
- [Kaori] They can't make me.

03:18.288 --> 03:20.290
- [Toshiro] I have to get more.
- I won't do it. It's mine.

03:20.373 --> 03:23.001
- [low electrical humming]
- [faint clacking]

03:30.300 --> 03:33.887
[Toshiro] <i>I work 14-hour shifts at</i>
<i>the factory for 90,000 yen a month.</i>

03:33.970 --> 03:36.598
<i>Rent is 30,000. Utilities, 5,000.</i>

03:36.681 --> 03:37.933
<i>Taxes,15,000.</i>

03:38.016 --> 03:39.809
<i>My mother's medication is 20,000.</i>

03:39.893 --> 03:42.145
<i>That leaves me less than 20,000 yen after.</i>

03:42.229 --> 03:45.357
<i>No matter how often I apply for welfare,</i>
<i>I never get approved.</i>

03:45.982 --> 03:47.317
[door clanging]

03:47.400 --> 03:49.778
<i>An inspection? Already?</i>

03:49.861 --> 03:50.862
SUPERVISOR OF AREA EAST 2

03:50.946 --> 03:51.988
[door slams loudly]

03:57.619 --> 03:59.120
<i>Shit, shit, shit.</i>

03:59.204 --> 04:01.331
<i>I've barely done anything yet.</i>
<i>I gotta hurry.</i>

04:01.414 --> 04:02.791
[creaking]

04:05.085 --> 04:08.380
<i>I've cut back on food expenses</i>
<i>to save 1,000 yen each month.</i>

04:08.463 --> 04:10.590
<i>I'm doing it so I can get a better job,</i>

04:10.674 --> 04:14.094
<i>but I need an education for that</i>
<i>and an education costs money.</i>

04:14.803 --> 04:16.096
<i>I can't stay here.</i>

04:16.179 --> 04:18.265
<i>I'll die if don't get a better job.</i>

04:20.183 --> 04:23.895
<i>I've worked here for three years</i>
<i>and I've only saved 20,000 yen.</i>

04:25.272 --> 04:26.606
[grunts in pain]

04:26.690 --> 04:28.149
[clattering]

04:38.576 --> 04:40.912
Don't even think about
getting paid for today.

04:48.128 --> 04:49.337
[yells in frustration]

04:51.798 --> 04:52.841
[sobbing]

04:54.551 --> 04:57.262
[protestors chanting]
Down with Transfloration!

04:57.345 --> 04:59.347
Down with Transfloration!

04:59.431 --> 05:01.516
Down with Transfloration!

05:01.599 --> 05:03.727
Down with Transfloration!

05:03.810 --> 05:06.021
Down with Transfloration!

05:06.104 --> 05:08.356
Down with Transfloration!

05:08.440 --> 05:10.567
Down with Transfloration!

05:10.650 --> 05:13.486
Down with Transfloration! Down with--

05:13.570 --> 05:14.404
PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

05:14.487 --> 05:15.989
[Toshiro sobbing] Please. I'm begging you.

05:16.573 --> 05:19.242
I need it for my mother.
For her… her medication.

05:19.326 --> 05:21.870
She gets violent without it
and I can't stop her.

05:21.953 --> 05:23.330
I swear, I'll pay you back.

05:24.581 --> 05:28.126
Last week, you said
the same exact thing to me.

05:28.710 --> 05:29.711
Get out of here.

05:38.595 --> 05:40.221
[melancholy music playing]

05:42.474 --> 05:44.434
KAORI & TOSHIRO KAMIYA

05:44.768 --> 05:45.894
[door creaks]

05:45.977 --> 05:47.187
[door shuts]

05:54.277 --> 05:56.321
[Toshiro]
The tuition money that I'd hidden.

05:56.404 --> 05:58.865
You lied. It was all a lie.

05:58.948 --> 06:01.701
You said you ran out of money,
but it was a lie!

06:01.785 --> 06:03.953
It wasn't! I swear!

06:04.037 --> 06:05.497
How dare you!

06:05.580 --> 06:08.041
Everyone is against me,
but I won't lose. I won't!

06:08.124 --> 06:10.293
That money's for
my high school tuition, Mom!

06:10.376 --> 06:13.463
- Why would you--
- I've had enough of your excuses!

06:13.546 --> 06:14.756
[Toshiro whimpering]

06:15.381 --> 06:16.841
[Toshiro grunting, panting]

06:18.802 --> 06:20.178
[panting]

06:21.221 --> 06:22.597
[Toshiro grunting, straining]

06:23.473 --> 06:25.266
[Kaori straining]

06:25.350 --> 06:26.267
[panting]

06:26.351 --> 06:28.061
[panting heavily]

06:28.144 --> 06:29.729
[panting]

06:29.813 --> 06:31.481
[melancholy music continues]

06:34.859 --> 06:36.277
[Kaori screaming]

06:44.410 --> 06:45.495
[grunting]

06:45.954 --> 06:47.330
[Kaori breathing heavily]

06:48.498 --> 06:49.541
[Toshiro] <i>Why?</i>

06:50.416 --> 06:51.960
<i>What did I do wrong?</i>

06:53.336 --> 06:54.879
<i>Why am I always the one suffering?</i>

06:57.090 --> 06:59.008
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

07:02.720 --> 07:04.055
[metallic clinking]

07:20.029 --> 07:22.449
[protestors chanting faintly]
Down with Transfloration!

07:22.532 --> 07:24.951
[female detective]
There have been more protests lately.

07:25.034 --> 07:26.453
[male detective] You know, if it were me,

07:26.536 --> 07:29.289
I'd be protesting
for better working conditions.

07:29.372 --> 07:31.833
I'd fight for overtime
for detectives, too.

07:31.916 --> 07:33.793
[protestors continue chanting
indistinctly]

07:33.877 --> 07:35.336
Looks like a mother and her child.

07:35.753 --> 07:37.255
Any sign of the culprit?

07:37.338 --> 07:39.424
We've looked around and there's nothing.

07:39.507 --> 07:41.426
It's pretty weird, huh? Don't you think?

07:41.509 --> 07:42.594
[static buzzing]

07:43.386 --> 07:45.138
[Jin, over phone]
<i>They asked for our help with a case</i>

07:45.221 --> 07:47.348
<i>they think is connected to Transfloration.</i>

07:47.432 --> 07:48.766
<i>Everyone else turned them down,</i>

07:48.850 --> 07:50.518
<i>but if you want to get ahead</i>
<i>in your career--</i>

07:50.602 --> 07:53.188
Yeah, I'll do it.
As long as I get paid extra.

07:53.271 --> 07:55.315
<i>Oh, uh, thanks.</i>

07:55.398 --> 07:58.818
[Yomiko] I have a Transfloration
application review so I gotta go.

08:00.403 --> 08:02.155
[sighs heavily]

08:03.364 --> 08:06.618
I wish I could just get 10 million yen
without working for it.

08:09.204 --> 08:11.164
[grunts, sighs]

08:11.247 --> 08:13.791
Let's get this over with so I can go eat.

08:17.712 --> 08:18.963
Hello.

08:19.714 --> 08:21.382
Oh, it's cold in here.

08:23.676 --> 08:25.011
[gasps softly]

08:31.309 --> 08:33.728
Oh, what are… I didn't realize it…

08:39.901 --> 08:42.237
[Toshiro sobs softly]

08:50.995 --> 08:52.413
[Yomiko] How long has it been?

08:55.250 --> 08:57.752
About 15 years, I think.

08:57.835 --> 09:00.880
But you never called though.
Did you not have a phone?

09:01.923 --> 09:03.675
Are you really going to die?

09:04.384 --> 09:07.804
Only people about to die can
have the procedure, isn't that right?

09:07.887 --> 09:09.973
I have a medical report from my doctor.

09:11.057 --> 09:12.976
SMALL INTESTINE CANCER

09:14.185 --> 09:18.606
I just want you to plant a Seed in my body
and turn me into a beautiful flower.

09:20.567 --> 09:24.362
[Yomiko] Well, first I need to run
a quick test to confirm this diagnosis.

09:37.667 --> 09:39.586
Did someone do that to you?

09:40.920 --> 09:43.047
This city gets more dangerous by the day.

09:43.131 --> 09:45.258
Not that it was ever great
when we were kids.

09:45.341 --> 09:46.843
[Toshiro] I'm fine.

09:47.343 --> 09:49.762
[machinery whirring, clacking]

09:53.975 --> 09:56.394
SAVE THE WORLD THROUGH TRANSFLORATION!

10:02.567 --> 10:03.943
[young Toshiro sobbing]

10:08.448 --> 10:11.242
Toshiro. Yomiko. Who did that to you?

10:11.659 --> 10:13.745
I'm gonna kill that old man.

10:15.163 --> 10:18.333
Why are all the adults in this world
so angry all the time?

10:18.958 --> 10:20.001
I'm so sick of it.

10:21.127 --> 10:23.546
Those clouds have cast a shadow
over everyone's hearts.

10:23.630 --> 10:27.300
They turn us against each other
and have narrowed our perspectives.

10:28.259 --> 10:30.428
Now, this might be
a little hard for you to understand,

10:30.511 --> 10:31.929
but keep your hearts open.

10:32.013 --> 10:34.349
Keep them open
and fill them with good things

10:34.432 --> 10:36.017
so you don't end up like that.

10:36.100 --> 10:37.685
I don't understand.

10:37.769 --> 10:38.978
I swear, I'll kill that guy.

10:39.062 --> 10:40.772
[machinery whirring, clacking]

10:45.735 --> 10:47.028
[gasps]

10:47.111 --> 10:48.237
[door opens]

10:48.988 --> 10:50.365
[footsteps approaching]

10:50.448 --> 10:51.449
[door closes]

10:53.326 --> 10:56.079
[Yomiko]
Why did you lie about having cancer?

10:56.162 --> 10:58.373
[Toshiro] You wouldn't approve me
if you knew it was suicide.

10:58.456 --> 11:02.377
[Yomiko] I found 150 types of chemicals
and bacteria in your blood.

11:02.460 --> 11:05.129
Did you put industrial wastewater
in your body

11:05.213 --> 11:07.090
just to get the Transfloration Subsidy?

11:07.173 --> 11:08.549
I'm taking you to the hospital.

11:08.633 --> 11:10.635
You could still be saved with dialysis.

11:11.928 --> 11:13.054
Let's go!

11:13.554 --> 11:15.390
[Toshiro]
I don't have enough money for that.

11:15.473 --> 11:17.100
I'm not a civil servant.

11:17.183 --> 11:20.353
A lot of people are doing this now though,
so why does it matter?

11:20.436 --> 11:22.105
Just sign it already.

11:22.188 --> 11:23.773
I could really use the money.

11:23.856 --> 11:25.900
I don't even have enough for food today.

11:25.983 --> 11:27.443
What's the point of all that if you die?

11:27.527 --> 11:30.446
I'm not actually dying.
It's Transfloration!

11:30.530 --> 11:32.407
I'm just tired of worrying about money.

11:32.490 --> 11:34.242
You want to end up like that?

11:34.325 --> 11:35.785
You won't be able to move an inch.

11:35.868 --> 11:37.286
All that's left is your consciousness

11:37.370 --> 11:39.163
while the plant keeps
feeding on your body!

11:39.247 --> 11:41.916
Sometimes they talk,
but no one can understand them.

11:42.542 --> 11:45.169
You might end up suffering the whole time.

11:45.253 --> 11:46.421
I don't care!

11:46.504 --> 11:48.589
I'm gonna fill my heart
with that 10 million yen.

11:48.673 --> 11:51.175
[melancholy music playing]

11:52.552 --> 11:53.928
Don't be ridiculous.

11:55.012 --> 11:57.682
There's nothing in this life
that brings me joy.

12:08.651 --> 12:09.652
Please.

12:11.237 --> 12:12.738
[melancholy music continues]

12:29.922 --> 12:31.507
[Yomiko] That guy who came in
the other day…

12:31.591 --> 12:32.884
- [receptionist] Hmm?
- Toshiro Kamiya.

12:32.967 --> 12:34.594
Did he go through with Transfloration?

12:34.677 --> 12:35.678
Kamiya?

12:38.306 --> 12:41.225
Yeah, it says he underwent
the procedure five days ago.

12:41.726 --> 12:42.894
[Yomiko] Thanks.

12:55.281 --> 12:56.157
[Yomiko] <i>Rain.</i>

12:58.493 --> 12:59.619
- [vehicle honks]
- [Yomiko] Uh-huh.

12:59.702 --> 13:01.204
I was just wondering how you were.

13:01.287 --> 13:03.539
It's been awhile.
We should go out for dinner again.

13:03.623 --> 13:04.957
Call me back, bye.

13:10.087 --> 13:11.547
[tense music playing]

13:14.634 --> 13:15.676
[gasps]

13:18.513 --> 13:19.805
Is that you, Yomiko?

13:22.475 --> 13:23.643
[Yomiko] What happened?

13:25.228 --> 13:27.313
[Toshiro] They took all of my money.

13:27.813 --> 13:29.190
[stomach growling]

13:32.485 --> 13:33.611
- [footsteps approaching]
- [gasps]

13:36.781 --> 13:37.823
Huh?

13:38.241 --> 13:39.408
[Toshiro grunts]

13:46.123 --> 13:48.042
- [sizzling]
- [rock music plays on speakers]

14:04.141 --> 14:05.351
Mmm.

14:17.321 --> 14:18.364
[grunts softly]

14:41.345 --> 14:42.471
So good.

14:42.555 --> 14:45.433
It's been such a long time since I've…
[sniffles] eaten meat.

14:47.226 --> 14:48.811
How much does it cost?

14:48.895 --> 14:50.897
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

14:52.773 --> 14:55.192
Food is one of the ways
I fill my heart. All of it.

14:55.776 --> 14:56.903
Uh…

14:58.112 --> 14:59.155
[thunder rumbling]

15:00.656 --> 15:03.576
Civil servants have it so good.
They make so much money.

15:08.080 --> 15:11.208
By the way, is my blood clean now?

15:11.292 --> 15:12.668
[Yomiko] Uh, yeah.

15:12.752 --> 15:15.755
I think the Seed purified
the industrial wastewater.

15:15.838 --> 15:18.257
The Seed has a strong ability
to repair its host.

15:18.341 --> 15:21.344
If you're concerned, we can go
and get it checked out tomorrow?

15:21.427 --> 15:23.220
Then maybe we can
eat out again, afterwards.

15:23.304 --> 15:24.889
It's fine, don't worry about me.

15:24.972 --> 15:26.766
Huh? No, I wasn't.

15:28.017 --> 15:29.560
Well, the one behind you,

15:30.645 --> 15:33.898
it says it senses self-blame
and regret coming from you.

15:37.318 --> 15:40.529
[Yomiko] You can understand them?
The Spiriflora?

15:41.364 --> 15:43.991
Can't everyone understand them
after Transfloration?

15:44.617 --> 15:46.786
No, they don't. I've never heard of that.

15:47.620 --> 15:48.996
So what are…

15:49.080 --> 15:51.499
[Toshiro] Now it says you have
some kind of expectation.

15:51.582 --> 15:52.750
[gasps]

15:53.376 --> 15:54.377
- We need to go…
- Huh?

15:54.460 --> 15:56.796
…to Transflora Medical. Like, right now.

15:57.380 --> 15:58.381
Uh-huh.

16:22.905 --> 16:24.699
[footsteps approaching]

16:29.203 --> 16:30.371
What are we doing here?

16:32.623 --> 16:33.749
Hello, there.

16:34.834 --> 16:36.752
I'm Jin Hiragishi from the Unsection.

16:38.838 --> 16:40.631
Unsection?

16:40.715 --> 16:44.218
Unsection handles anything
that's related to Transfloration.

16:44.719 --> 16:45.970
- He's a higher up.
- [gasps]

16:46.053 --> 16:48.556
Well I'm Toshiro Kamiya.

16:48.639 --> 16:50.766
So, you can understand Spiriflora?

16:51.225 --> 16:52.476
You told him?

16:52.560 --> 16:54.812
He can hear them and he can sense
what people are feeling

16:54.895 --> 16:56.522
when Spiriflora are nearby.

16:56.605 --> 16:58.149
He's a perfect fit for us.

16:58.232 --> 17:00.568
He might even be able to help
with that case.

17:00.651 --> 17:01.819
[Jin] Hmm.

17:02.361 --> 17:04.030
What are you talking about?

17:04.113 --> 17:07.199
I'm talking about hiring you
as a temporary worker here.

17:07.283 --> 17:08.284
Huh?

17:08.367 --> 17:10.828
Look, if you work here,
you're going to make good money

17:10.911 --> 17:12.371
for your last two years as a human.

17:12.455 --> 17:14.373
Not a bad deal, right?

17:14.457 --> 17:17.793
Well… well, yeah. I mean,
I would do anything to make more money.

17:17.877 --> 17:19.336
I didn't hire you yet.

17:19.962 --> 17:22.506
You can't expect me to just believe you.

17:22.590 --> 17:23.883
Is it really true?

17:23.966 --> 17:25.718
Well, yeah. For the most part.

17:25.801 --> 17:28.512
I don't hear words. It's more like
I sense what they're feeling.

17:28.596 --> 17:31.223
Do Spiriflora themselves
have personalities?

17:31.307 --> 17:32.808
What do they say when no one's around?

17:32.892 --> 17:34.894
Well, it depends on the individual.

17:35.895 --> 17:37.229
Some of them scream.

17:37.313 --> 17:38.355
Some just want water.

17:38.439 --> 17:40.191
But, I'm not able to hear anything

17:40.274 --> 17:43.110
from the ones that have
been Spiriflora for a long time.

17:43.194 --> 17:45.029
[static buzzing]

17:45.112 --> 17:47.531
Okay, so what are they
sensing from me right now?

17:48.657 --> 17:53.370
They sense confusion,
expectations, resignation.

17:54.121 --> 17:56.749
Also, self-criticism.

17:59.627 --> 18:00.669
[Jin] Come with me.

18:00.753 --> 18:03.047
[footsteps]

18:04.298 --> 18:05.132
Where are we going?

18:05.216 --> 18:07.635
So you automatically understand
their voices, huh?

18:07.718 --> 18:11.013
Mm. I mean, it's not really like that.

18:11.097 --> 18:14.225
I would say it's almost like
a feeling that just comes through.

18:16.727 --> 18:19.063
You see this?
This is one of my old colleagues.

18:19.647 --> 18:21.816
Tell me what it's saying. Is it screaming?

18:21.899 --> 18:23.484
I don't understand all of them.

18:23.567 --> 18:25.402
[static buzzing]

18:29.698 --> 18:31.408
I'm sorry. I don't know.

18:31.492 --> 18:33.244
I'm sure it's saying something though.

18:33.327 --> 18:35.371
- You're hired if you can hear it.
- [gasps]

18:35.454 --> 18:37.164
You better not make it up, either.

18:37.248 --> 18:41.669
Even without having a power like yours,
I'm able to tell if somebody's lying.

18:42.169 --> 18:43.295
[heart thumping]

18:45.881 --> 18:49.426
[Toshiro] <i>If I can't hear it,</i>
<i>if I don't get hired,</i>

18:49.510 --> 18:52.346
<i>how will I survive any longer</i>
<i>in that house?</i>

18:52.429 --> 18:54.014
[melancholy music playing]

18:54.557 --> 18:55.683
[sighs]

18:57.852 --> 18:59.019
[heart continues thumping]

19:00.604 --> 19:02.273
[music continues]

19:19.206 --> 19:21.208
<i>I have no choice but to listen.</i>

19:23.002 --> 19:24.211
<i>Listen!</i>

19:27.006 --> 19:28.215
<i>I know I can hear it.</i>

19:29.091 --> 19:30.467
<i>Listen harder!</i>

19:33.554 --> 19:34.847
<i>Focus on it!</i>

19:35.890 --> 19:37.099
[grunting]

19:37.892 --> 19:39.602
[voices overlapping]

19:40.603 --> 19:41.770
[grunting]

19:41.854 --> 19:44.440
- [woman] <i>Why is this hurting so much?</i>
- [voices overlap]

19:46.025 --> 19:47.234
[sobbing]

19:51.614 --> 19:53.032
[inaudible]

19:53.115 --> 19:55.075
[stifled sobbing]

20:02.249 --> 20:05.169
[male voice] <i>Go… Go to…</i>

20:06.170 --> 20:07.755
Go… Go to…

20:08.839 --> 20:10.132
<i>Antarctica.</i>

20:10.216 --> 20:11.091
[echoing]

20:11.175 --> 20:12.301
Antarctica.

20:18.891 --> 20:21.018
I heard you have no place to sleep.

20:22.770 --> 20:25.189
Come here at the same time tomorrow.

20:25.272 --> 20:26.482
- [Toshiro] Huh?
- [Jin] Hmm.

20:26.565 --> 20:28.442
Uh… [stuttering] Okay, thank you.

20:40.871 --> 20:41.956
[grunts softly]

20:44.833 --> 20:47.211
[retching]

20:47.294 --> 20:48.170
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

20:48.254 --> 20:49.880
[Yomiko] What's wrong?
I need paper towels!

20:49.964 --> 20:51.173
[Toshiro] My head's pounding.

20:51.257 --> 20:54.218
What the hell was that feeling?
I'm never doing that again.

20:55.803 --> 20:57.846
[receptionist] Including the unpaid
balance from last time…

20:57.930 --> 20:58.847
NIKONIKO PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

20:58.931 --> 21:00.641
…that'll be 35,000 yen.

21:03.394 --> 21:04.603
Huh?

21:06.563 --> 21:07.564
Hmm.

21:08.524 --> 21:10.776
ORAL MEDICATION
KAORI KAMIYA, THREE TIMES A DAY

21:10.859 --> 21:13.279
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

21:14.571 --> 21:17.533
As long as you have the money,
I won't complain.

21:17.616 --> 21:18.701
[door shuts]

21:18.993 --> 21:20.327
[sighs deeply]

21:28.043 --> 21:29.044
[gasps]

21:30.462 --> 21:31.964
[rock music playing]

21:39.263 --> 21:40.931
[Yomiko] Is that what you wanted?

21:41.015 --> 21:42.349
[Toshiro] Huh?

21:42.433 --> 21:43.892
To spend your money on that?

21:46.770 --> 21:50.441
Are you going home to give that medicine
to your mom now?

21:54.403 --> 21:55.696
[Toshiro] How much will I get paid?

21:55.779 --> 21:57.281
Well, I think, um…

21:57.364 --> 22:00.701
uh, temp workers get
150,000 plus benefits.

22:00.784 --> 22:02.578
[Toshiro] That's double
what I used to make.

22:04.413 --> 22:06.749
From now on, I can eat out every day.

22:07.833 --> 22:11.128
And I can try new foods
that I've never been able to before.

22:12.755 --> 22:13.839
Toshiro…

22:14.548 --> 22:15.758
And I…

22:17.092 --> 22:18.302
And I…

22:20.054 --> 22:21.096
Oh, whoa!

22:21.180 --> 22:22.765
[rock music continues]

22:26.894 --> 22:28.228
[panting]

22:31.774 --> 22:32.858
[gasps]

22:39.198 --> 22:41.325
[rock music continues]

23:04.890 --> 23:05.766
Let's go.

23:12.064 --> 23:13.107
Thank you for this.

23:13.732 --> 23:15.692
[rock music continues]

23:32.000 --> 23:34.002
[rock music continues]

24:00.988 --> 24:02.990
[ominous music playing]
